\subsubsection{Step 3: Laminar Family $\lset$ of Clusters,  and Internal and External Routers for Clusters of $\lset$}

For each $1\le i\le r$, we define cluster $U_i$ to be the subgraph of $G$ induced by $\bigcup_{1\le z\le i}V(\tilde S_z)$. For convenience, we also denote by $\notU_i$ the subgraph of $G$ induced by $\bigcup_{i< z\le r}V(\tilde S_z)$. We then define a laminar family $\lset=\set{U_1,\ldots,U_r}$ of clusters of $G$. Notice that $U_r=G$, and $U_1\subseteq U_2\subseteq\cdots\subseteq U_r$. 

